# My openElement App

Generated by [`@openelement/create`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@openelement/create).
A file-based openElement app: page routes live in `app/routes/`, compiled page
elements and shared style sheets in `app/components/`, and client islands
(including the `app-shell` layout island) in `app/islands/`.

This starter pins the exact `@openelement/element` and `@openelement/router`
versions it was generated from (`${v.element}`) in `package.json`; update both
there when moving to a new release.

Styling ownership is split three ways. Global design tokens and the document
baseline (`body`, `::selection`) live in `app/styles/tokens.css` — the file
convention the build inlines into every document `<head>`. Pages use light
roots and own their rules in `static styles`
(`app/components/page-styles.ts`): the server inlines each page's sheets into
the SSR output as a `@scope(<page-tag>)` style block, so pages are fully styled
with zero client JavaScript. The shell and the islands hydrate in the browser
and carry their own `static styles`.

## Where options live

Framework options have exactly one home: `openelement.config.ts`. It is
optional and nearly empty — every option it omits comes from a file
convention:

| Option | Convention |
| --- | --- |
| design tokens | `app/styles/tokens.css` |
| app shell | `app/islands/app-shell.tsx` (deletable) |
| document head content | `app/head.tsx` (meta tags, preloads, inline CSS) |
| site title | the `name` field of `package.json` |

Passing framework options inline to `openElement()` while the config file
carries options is a hard error, and an unknown key fails the build with the
accepted-key list. `vite.config.ts` stays Vite-only: `plugins: [...openElement()]`.
The conventions follow the `dirs` block, so moving the three roots under
`src/` moves the token, shell and head files with them.

## Scripts

- `pnpm dev` — start the Vite dev server.
- `pnpm check` — type-check every route/component file. The check covers the
  whole `app/` directory (`tsconfig.json`), so new files are picked up
  automatically.
- `pnpm test` — run Node's built-in test runner (the starter ships none).
- `pnpm build` — production build (SSG + Nitro server) into `dist/`.
- `pnpm start` — serve the production build. Use this for production
  preview: the starter ships a request-time route (`/contact`), so
  `pnpm preview` (static-only preview, #601) is refused by design.
- `pnpm preview` — static-only preview; refused for this starter (see
  above).

## Blog

Blog posts are compiled page routes: `app/routes/blog/welcome.tsx` renders at
`/blog/welcome`, prerendered at build time. Add a post by creating a page
element under `app/components/` and a route module under `app/routes/blog/`,
then link it from `app/routes/blog/index.tsx` (the index list is static
authoring). Interactive content belongs in a compiled island composed from
the page.

## Dependency notes

`hono` and `@hono/vite-dev-server` are installed even though no source file
imports them: the dev server resolves `hono` when loading the generated
server entry (the bundled `dist/` output inlines it). For Nitro deployments,
the built handler bridges through the `@openelement/router/nitro-mount`
subpath of the one `@openelement/router` dependency. Do not remove them.

## Brand assets

`public/openelement-mark.svg` is the openElement brand mark shipped with the
starter — use it for a favicon or page header, or delete it if unused.
